//==
// # Implicit shape interfaces
//
// Shapes described by functions rather than boundaries. A signed distance
// field (SDF; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Signed_distance_function) reports
// how far a point is from a surface, negative inside; an implicit region
// reports only membership (see also https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Implicit_surface).
// The concrete types implementing these interfaces are declared in
// `implicit-sdf.types.plato`.
//
// Unbounded vs bounded: `ISignedDistanceField2D/3D` are pure distance oracles
// with no finite domain. `IBoundedSignedDistanceField2D/3D` add a conservative
// AABB (`IBounded2D/3D`) for culling and acceleration; `DistanceAt` /
// `Eval` still evaluate the underlying field everywhere — bounds are hints,
// not a change to distance semantics. Analytic wrappers live in
// `implicit-sdf.types.plato`; sampled lattices (`SampledSdf*`) already
// carry a `Bounds` spanning their finite support and implement the bounded
// interfaces.
//
// Differentiable: `IDifferentiableSignedDistanceField2D/3D` add a gradient, which
// for a distance field is the outward normal direction. They inherit
// `IDifferentiableScalarField2D/3D` (`fields.concepts.plato`), so every helper
// derived from a gradient there — `SurfaceNormalAt`, `BoundaryNormalAt`,
// `SlopeAt` — resolves against an SDF that reports one. Reporting a gradient is
// a separate claim from reporting a distance: a field whose values are only
// conservative lower bounds still has a gradient, but it is not the surface
// normal.

// A planar scalar field whose value is the signed distance to a boundary
// curve: negative inside, zero on the boundary, positive outside. Values are
// exact distances or conservative lower bounds of them.
interface ISignedDistanceField2D
    inherits IScalarField2D
{ }

// A spatial scalar field whose value is the signed distance to a surface:
// negative inside, zero on the surface, positive outside. Values are exact
// distances or conservative lower bounds of them.
interface ISignedDistanceField3D
    inherits IScalarField3D
{ }

// A planar SDF plus a conservative axis-aligned domain for culling. Bounds
// should enclose every point where distance ≤ 0 when used as a solid hint;
// for sampled lattices they span the lattice. Outside Bounds, callers may
// skip work; Eval / DistanceAt remain defined and unchanged.
interface IBoundedSignedDistanceField2D
    inherits ISignedDistanceField2D, IBounded2D
{ }

// A spatial SDF plus a conservative axis-aligned domain for culling. Same
// semantics as the planar form: Bounds are acceleration hints, not a clamp
// on distance evaluation.
interface IBoundedSignedDistanceField3D
    inherits ISignedDistanceField3D, IBounded3D
{ }

// A planar SDF that reports a gradient as well as a distance. For an exact
// distance field the unit gradient is the outward normal of the boundary curve,
// and the gradient has unit length wherever the field is differentiable
// (the eikonal property, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eikonal_equation).
// The gradient is undefined on the seam of a Min/Max combination, where the
// implementor reports one side's gradient rather than failing.
interface IDifferentiableSignedDistanceField2D
    inherits ISignedDistanceField2D, IDifferentiableScalarField2D
{ }

// A spatial SDF that reports a gradient as well as a distance. For an exact
// distance field the unit gradient is the outward surface normal. Same seam
// caveat as the planar form.
interface IDifferentiableSignedDistanceField3D
    inherits ISignedDistanceField3D, IDifferentiableScalarField3D
{ }

// A planar region described by a membership predicate: true when the point
// is inside. Carries no distance information.
interface IImplicitRegion2D
    inherits IProcedural<Point2D, Boolean>
{ }

// A spatial volume described by a membership predicate: true when the point
// is inside. Carries no distance information.
interface IImplicitVolume3D
    inherits IProcedural<Point3D, Boolean>
{ }
